warning[returned_local_address]: this pointer refers to stack storage whose lifetime has ended
  --> tests/lint/pointer_lifetime/resources/bad.jai:78:18
   |
73 |     {
   |     - storage invalidated here
   ...
75 |         p = *value;
   |             ------ storage derived here
   ...
78 |     print("%\n", p.*);
   |                  ^
   |
   = help: keep the value in the enclosing scope, or copy it into caller-owned storage
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/returned_local_address

warning[returned_local_address]: the address of the local `it` escapes into storage that outlives it
  --> tests/lint/pointer_lifetime/resources/bad.jai:83:26
   |
83 |     for values escaped = *it;
   |                          ^^^
   |                          --- stack storage borrowed here
   |
   = help: return the value itself, take the memory from an allocator (`New`, `alloc`), or have the caller pass the place to fill
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/returned_local_address

